    {
      "id": "F11",
      "statement": "What tells the alerts apart: as indicators the six are alike (5 to 8 distinct senders in one hour, one transfer per sender). The recorded relationships differ. (a) Onward links: A-28137 has none. A-85921 and A-20636 have one link each, to a single account, and some of their credits are unlinked. A-10859, A-37573 and A-83577 have multi-link paths of depth 3, 4 and 5, and every one of their contributing transfers starts a path. (b) Shared devices on the paths: A-37573's paths use one device, D-45880, across four of its five path accounts. A-10859's alerted account and first path account share D-79802. A-83577 has two non-adjacent path accounts on D-40018, which one outside account also used. A-85921, A-28137 and A-20636 have no shared device on their paths. (c) Amounts: A-85921 received six transfers of exactly 2500 each. A-37573's two path sequences repeat the same account order.",
